---
import ServiceCard from "../../components/cards/ServiceCard.astro";
import ProcessTimeline from "../../components/sections/ProcessTimeline.astro";
import CtaSection from "../../components/sections/CtaSection.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../../components/ui/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import { getService, serviceFlow, serviceNeeds, services } from "../../data/services";
import { processSteps } from "../../data/process";
import { assets } from "../../data/assets";
import { site } from "../../data/site";
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const linkedNeeds = serviceNeeds.map((need) => ({
  ...need,
  services: need.slugs.map((slug) => {
    const service = getService(slug);
    if (!service) throw new Error(`Missing service for need: ${slug}`);
    return service;
  }),
}));
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`Software Services | ${site.name}`}
  description={`${site.name} helps startups with web development, mobile apps, AI, SaaS, backend APIs, cloud delivery, product design, and software testing.`}
  fullTitle
>
  <section class="relative isolate overflow-hidden pt-28 pb-16 md:pt-32">
    <img class="scene-wash" src={assets.backgrounds.servicesSpheres} alt="" width="1920" height="800" />
    <div class="container-page relative z-[1]">
      <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: "Home", href: "/" }, { label: "Services" }]} />
      <p class="eyebrow">Our expertise</p>
      <h1 class="page-title mt-5 max-w-4xl">Software Development for <span class="text-gradient">Ambitious Startups.</span></h1>
      <p class="lede mt-6 max-w-3xl">
        From web and mobile applications to AI-powered systems and scalable infrastructure, {site.name} brings together the technical capabilities needed to plan, build, and improve software products.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section reveal pt-0" aria-labelledby="directory-heading">
    <div class="container-page">
      <h2 id="directory-heading" class="section-title">Eight ways a product gets built.</h2>
      <p class="lede mt-4 max-w-3xl">Each practice has its own page. The names match the work. A proposal decides the slice. Nothing on this page is included automatically.</p>
      <div class="mt-12 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">
        {services.map((service) => <ServiceCard service={service} detailed />)}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section reveal bg-ink-soft/40" aria-labelledby="needs-heading">
    <div class="container-page">
      <h2 id="needs-heading" class="section-title max-w-3xl">Startup development needs.</h2>
      <p class="lede mt-4 max-w-3xl">These are situations founders describe. The links show which practices usually apply. They are not case studies, and they are not a claim that a particular company has already been helped.</p>
      <div class="mt-10 grid gap-4">
        {
          linkedNeeds.map((need) => (
            <article class="surface-card p-6 md:p-8">
              <h3 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold">{need.title}</h3>
              <p class="mt-3 max-w-3xl text-muted">{need.text}</p>
              <ul class="mt-5 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
                {need.services.map((service) => (
                  <li>
                    <a class="tech-chip hover:text-paper" href={`/services/${service.slug}`}>{service.title}</a>
                  </li>
                ))}
              </ul>
            </article>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section reveal" aria-labelledby="together-heading">
    <div class="container-page grid items-start gap-x-[min(2.5rem,4vw)] gap-y-10 lg:grid-cols-12">
      <div class="lg:col-span-5">
        <h2 id="together-heading" class="section-title">How the services fit together.</h2>
        <div class="mt-6 grid gap-4 text-paper/90">
          <p>A startup product is rarely one specialty. Design names the task. A web or mobile client is what people touch. The backend holds the rules and the integrations. Cloud work is how that software gets to an environment someone else can deploy. Testing is the record of what was checked before anyone calls it ready.</p>
          <p>You do not have to buy all five layers. The useful question is which boundary is missing. A polished interface on top of undefined rules, or a deploy only one person can perform, is the usual place a first product stalls.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <ol class="grid gap-3 lg:col-span-7">
        {
          serviceFlow.map((step, index) => (
            <li class="surface-card flex gap-4 p-5">
              <span class="flex-none font-display text-lg font-semibold text-lilac">{String(index + 1).padStart(2, "0")}</span>
              <span>
                <span class="block font-display text-xl font-semibold">{step.title}</span>
                <span class="mt-1 block text-muted">{step.text}</span>
              </span>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section reveal bg-ink-soft/40" aria-labelledby="process-heading">
    <div class="container-page">
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-end justify-between gap-6">
        <div class="max-w-3xl">
          <h2 id="process-heading" class="section-title">The same six stages.</h2>
          <p class="lede mt-4">Service work follows the process already published: discovery, architecture, design, development, validation, and deployment. The process page has the detail.</p>
        </div>
        <a href="/process" class="font-semibold text-lavender">See the full process</a>
      </div>
      <div class="mt-10">
        <ProcessTimeline steps={processSteps.map((step) => ({ ...step, homeTitle: step.title }))} compact />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaSection
    title="Let's Talk About Your Product."
    description="Tell us what you are trying to ship. We will ask about the product, the constraints, and which of these practices actually apply."
    href="/contact"
    label="Discuss Your Project"
  />
</BaseLayout>
